  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0029","idiomatic","At the Kui meeting, Duke Huan wished to renege on Cao Mo's agreement, but Guan Zhong therefore kept faith with it, and the feudal lords therefore turned to Qi.","At the Ke meeting, Duke Huan wished to renege on Cao Mo's agreement, but Guan Zhong therefore kept faith with it, and the feudal lords therefore turned to Qi.","於柯之會 names the meeting place 柯, whose standard pinyin is Ke; Kui is a mistransliteration, and the proposed Ke replacement is otherwise unchanged and accurate.","high","applied"],
    ["s0029","literal","At the Kui meeting, Duke Huan wished to renege on Cao Mo's agreement, Guan Zhong therefore kept faith with it, the feudal lords therefore turned to Qi.","At the Ke meeting, Duke Huan wished to renege on Cao Mo's agreement, Guan Zhong therefore kept faith with it, the feudal lords therefore turned to Qi.","The literal field likewise misrenders 柯 as Kui; correcting to Ke matches the Chinese place name without other semantic change.","high","applied"]
  ],
